Receptionist 1, originally just named ''Receptionist'', was added in '''Beta 7.6'''. It was renamed to Receptionist 1 after [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Receptionist_2 Receptionist 2] was added in '''Beta 9.1'''.

It used to gain 1 gold for every kill it made, but this was reworked in '''Beta 9.3'''. Now, it gives 1 gold for every time it gets damaged, no matter how much that damage is, for the cost of 7G instead of 6G. '''Beta 10.2''' returned the cost to 6G.

'''Beta 13.1''' buffed it again. While it gained -1/-1 to end up with 3/5, it now gives 2 gold whenever it gets damaged. '''Beta 20.2''' reworked the effect by now reducing the cost of a random card in your hand by 2 instead of giving you 2 gold. This can also affect cards that are 0-1G, making it more risky to use.
